---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="Harbor Legal Independent Index" activeNav="home">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Public preview</p>
      <h1>See what's moving in American law, right now.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Bills are introduced, amended, and signed into law every day across all 50 states and
        Congress. Appeals courts and the Supreme Court hand down rulings that reshape how those
        laws are read. Harbor Legal Independent Index tracks all of it — so you can follow what's
        happening without having to go looking for it.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn btn-accent" href="/search/">Browse the index</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/reports/">Latest reports</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/method/">What we cover</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <article class="surface">
          <div class="card-label">Legislation</div>
          <div class="card-value">Bills in motion</div>
          <p class="card-copy">
            Every state legislature and Congress, tracked daily. See what's been introduced,
            what's moved through committee, what passed, and what was signed — across any
            state or the whole country at once.
          </p>
          <div class="card-actions">
            <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/search/">Browse bills</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="surface">
          <div class="card-label">Case law</div>
          <div class="card-value">Court signals</div>
          <p class="card-copy">
            Federal appeals circuits and the Supreme Court, including orders, cert grants, and
            opinions. When a ruling changes how a law is read, it shows up here alongside the
            legislation it touches.
          </p>
          <div class="card-actions">
            <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/search/">Browse courts</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="surface">
          <div class="card-label">By topic</div>
          <div class="card-value">Areas of law</div>
          <p class="card-copy">
            Follow a legal domain — housing, privacy, firearms, labor — and see every bill and
            ruling that touches it, across every jurisdiction, without piecing it together
            yourself.
          </p>
          <div class="card-actions">
            <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/search/">Browse by area</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">What surfaces</p>
          <h2>The kind of signals the index catches</h2>
        </div>
        <a href="/search/">Browse the index -&gt;</a>
      </div>
      <div class="surface">
        <div class="signal-stack">
          <div class="signal-item">A circuit court ruling changed how a federal privacy statute applies to state agencies — bills in three states are now being amended in response.</div>
          <div class="signal-item">Fourteen state legislatures introduced nearly identical housing bills in the same two-week window — one has already cleared committee.</div>
          <div class="signal-item">The Supreme Court granted cert on a case about administrative rulemaking authority — related legislation is now stalled in Congress pending the outcome.</div>
          <div class="signal-item">A law signed in California is being used as a template in five other states — the same language is showing up in bills introduced this session.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Where this is going</p>
          <h2>What gets added as the index grows</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="roadmap-grid">
        <article class="roadmap-step">
          <div class="card-label">Now</div>
          <h3>Bills across all 50 states and Congress</h3>
          <p>Daily collection from every state legislature and Congress.gov, normalized into a single index you can browse or search.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="roadmap-step">
          <div class="card-label">Next</div>
          <h3>Court opinions connected to legislation</h3>
          <p>Appeals circuit and SCOTUS rulings linked to the bills and statutes they interpret, so you can see how case law is reshaping active legislation.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="roadmap-step">
          <div class="card-label">Later</div>
          <h3>Browse and follow by area of law</h3>
          <p>Pick a legal domain — housing, labor, privacy — and see everything moving in that space across every jurisdiction, without constructing the view yourself.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="roadmap-step">
          <div class="card-label">Future</div>
          <h3>Alerts and saved views</h3>
          <p>Get notified when something you care about moves. Watch a bill, follow a state, or track a topic area and receive updates when the index changes.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
